  "reason": "The strongest evidence is config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted fusion, with the best validation accuracy and F1. Weighted fusion also consistently outperformed concat, and multiprofile avgpool helped in RNA-only models. The main uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation is actually needed in the multimodal setting, since singleprofile multimodal with the same weighted PCA-ResNet design is untested. config_017 tests this by switching to singleprofile while keeping the best-supported fusion, image encoder, and RNA encoder. It is a high-value next step because it exploits the current best direction, may produce a competitive simpler model, and clarifies whether multiprofile complexity is worth retaining under a limited budget."
}

